- [Joey] Mm.

01:13:47.055 --> 01:13:48.953
- And if I would still feel the same way,

01:13:48.953 --> 01:13:51.450
or if I would still be desensitized,

01:13:51.450 --> 01:13:53.845
because it is a fictional story

01:13:53.845 --> 01:13:57.516
that has been told many, many, many times.

01:13:57.516 --> 01:13:58.830
- I think when it gets
to that point, though,

01:13:58.830 --> 01:14:03.073
it just revolves around how well written

01:14:03.073 --> 01:14:03.906
those stories and characters are.

01:14:03.906 --> 01:14:04.739
- That's true, that's true.

01:14:04.739 --> 01:14:07.380
- There are so many stories
where they use that trope.

01:14:07.380 --> 01:14:09.047
but you're just like,

01:14:09.047 --> 01:14:11.070
"Okay, I know I'm supposed to feel sad

01:14:11.070 --> 01:14:12.000
for this character right now,

01:14:12.000 --> 01:14:13.830
but the writing is so mediocre

01:14:13.830 --> 01:14:18.120
that it hasn't given me
enough emotional storage

01:14:18.120 --> 01:14:19.500
for me to care about this character.

01:14:19.500 --> 01:14:20.333
- That's true, that's true.

01:14:20.333 --> 01:14:23.070
- I think it's impossible to replicate

01:14:23.070 --> 01:14:24.960
the feeling of going
through it in real life,

01:14:24.960 --> 01:14:26.790
just because no matter
how good the writing is,

01:14:26.790 --> 01:14:29.073
'cause you know, you're talking about,

01:14:30.000 --> 01:14:31.070
let's say it's a movie.
- Yeah.

01:14:31.070 --> 01:14:32.730
- He tries to do it in two hours,

01:14:32.730 --> 01:14:36.360
what would take essentially
a lifetime to build up?

01:14:36.360 --> 01:14:37.193
- Yeah. Yeah.

01:14:37.193 --> 01:14:40.080
- The reason it's so
crippling in real life

01:14:40.080 --> 01:14:41.250
and it hurts so much,

01:14:41.250 --> 01:14:44.760
is because if it's your
friend and it happens at 20.

01:14:44.760 --> 01:14:46.200
It's like, alright, well you have 20 years

01:14:46.200 --> 01:14:48.390
of being their friend.

01:14:48.390 --> 01:14:51.480
And now it feels like it's being robbed.

01:14:51.480 --> 01:14:53.160
So I feel like it's almost impossible

01:14:53.160 --> 01:14:56.130
to portray it in a way that
will give you the same emotion.

01:14:56.130 --> 01:14:58.366
I think it can give you a sense of empathy

01:14:58.366 --> 01:15:00.030
in a very deep way,

01:15:00.030 --> 01:15:03.180
but nowhere near can it
compare to the feeling

01:15:03.180 --> 01:15:04.590
that you might feel if you go through it?

01:15:04.590 --> 01:15:05.430
I think.
- Yeah.

01:15:05.430 --> 01:15:08.430
- Well, I think one of
the biggest, not issues,

01:15:08.430 --> 01:15:10.260
but one of the biggest hurdles

01:15:10.260 --> 01:15:12.750
between communicating your experiences

01:15:12.750 --> 01:15:15.270
to an audience member or to someone

01:15:15.270 --> 01:15:16.800
who hasn't experienced
the same thing as you,

01:15:16.800 --> 01:15:19.500
is that there is such a massive difference

01:15:19.500 --> 01:15:22.053
between sympathy and empathy.

01:15:24.090 --> 01:15:25.140
There'll be people I talk to

01:15:25.140 --> 01:15:26.490
and they talk about their experiences

01:15:26.490 --> 01:15:28.020
and I can definitely sympathize

01:15:28.020 --> 01:15:30.060
with the emotion that they're feeling,

01:15:30.060 --> 01:15:32.820
but there's also like...

01:15:32.820 --> 01:15:35.160
do you guys ever feel a
connection with someone

01:15:35.160 --> 01:15:39.360
who has actually shared the
same experience with you,

01:15:39.360 --> 01:15:41.520
the same emotional experience with you?

01:15:41.520 --> 01:15:44.010
There's a connection there
when you share that experience

01:15:44.010 --> 01:15:45.510
that cannot be replicated

01:15:45.510 --> 01:15:47.790
no matter how much other people

01:15:47.790 --> 01:15:48.930
will try to understand you

01:15:48.930 --> 01:15:50.280
and try to understand your feelings

01:15:50.280 --> 01:15:51.930
and everything like that.

01:15:51.930 --> 01:15:54.480
There is a feeling that
cannot be replicated

01:15:54.480 --> 01:15:56.463
without the same empathy.

01:15:59.880 --> 01:16:01.680
To me there's something special

01:16:01.680 --> 01:16:04.920
about being able to
communicate that empathy

01:16:04.920 --> 01:16:07.560
through fictional media. Right?

01:16:07.560 --> 01:16:10.420
'Cause there are some
times where I watch a film

01:16:11.340 --> 01:16:13.387
and I feel something that's not just,

01:16:13.387 --> 01:16:16.620
"Hey, you should cry
or you should feel this

01:16:16.620 --> 01:16:18.030
because this character went through that.

01:16:18.030 --> 01:16:21.810
It's wow, I really feel
like an actual connection

01:16:21.810 --> 01:16:22.830
with the creator now

01:16:22.830 --> 01:16:25.110
because he's portraying an emotion

01:16:25.110 --> 01:16:27.960
that I know is impossible to depict

01:16:27.960 --> 01:16:31.470
unless you have been through
that exact experience.

01:16:31.470 --> 01:16:32.303
- [Joey] Yeah.

01:16:32.303 --> 01:16:33.180
- And I'm trying to feel,

01:16:33.180 --> 01:16:36.423
I'm trying to think of
when was the latest time,

01:16:37.860 --> 01:16:39.015
I mean off the top of my head,

01:16:39.015 --> 01:16:43.550
I think of "Evangelion", right,

01:16:45.120 --> 01:16:48.087
why I have such a close,
emotional connection to that.

01:16:48.087 --> 01:16:49.590
And it's so weird for me with "Ava"

01:16:49.590 --> 01:16:53.250
because I've watched "Ava"
in several stages of my life.

01:16:53.250 --> 01:16:56.670
And the reason it's the
most important for me

01:16:56.670 --> 01:16:58.290
was because there was a point

01:16:58.290 --> 01:17:00.690
where I felt like I was going through

01:17:00.690 --> 01:17:03.390
the exact same emotions the creator was,

01:17:03.390 --> 01:17:07.023
and this is going on a complete
fucking tangent, by the way.

01:17:07.970 --> 01:17:11.073
And yeah, I guess to me, that's why,

01:17:12.330 --> 01:17:14.400
going on a different tangent,

01:17:14.400 --> 01:17:18.480
that's why media is such
a big part of my life

01:17:18.480 --> 01:17:20.730
and why I'm a fucking
anime YouTuber, I guess,

01:17:20.730 --> 01:17:24.630
is because, I guess, that's
what I search for in media,

01:17:24.630 --> 01:17:25.920
which is not just to be entertained,

01:17:25.920 --> 01:17:29.820
but this connection with
a person and a creator.

01:17:29.820 --> 01:17:31.670
And that's why I try to make content.

01:17:32.872 --> 01:17:35.899
And I dunno where to go
from there, but that was-

01:17:35.899 --> 01:17:37.170
- Thank you for coming to my Ted Talk.

01:17:37.170 --> 01:17:40.200
- Thank you for coming
to my Ted Talk. Wow.

01:17:40.200 --> 01:17:41.477
I guess this is where you go

01:17:41.477 --> 01:17:43.662
from talking about people
dying from cancer, right?

01:17:43.662 --> 01:17:45.243
Where do you go from here?

01:17:46.140 --> 01:17:46.973
- Yeah, I dunno.

01:17:48.190 --> 01:17:52.290
It's tough because I think the one emotion

01:17:52.290 --> 01:17:54.240
that I personally feel

01:17:54.240 --> 01:17:57.551
when it comes to real life
situations and stuff like that,

01:17:57.551 --> 01:17:59.130
it's not even like...

01:17:59.130 --> 01:18:01.020
'cause you know, when
you're watching media

01:18:01.020 --> 01:18:03.270
that revolves around a
death of a character,

01:18:03.270 --> 01:18:06.720
in any situation, most
people think of sadness.

01:18:06.720 --> 01:18:11.720
You know, like a depression
or some rooted emotion.

01:18:13.560 --> 01:18:15.660
People who have experienced,
at least for me,

01:18:15.660 --> 01:18:19.804
when I experience a
real death that happened

01:18:19.804 --> 01:18:22.290
you don't feel anything.

01:18:22.290 --> 01:18:24.380
It's like you feel empty.

01:18:24.380 --> 01:18:25.213
- Yeah.

01:18:25.213 --> 01:18:27.840
- And I think this feeling of emptiness

01:18:27.840 --> 01:18:32.340
is extremely difficult
to portray in fiction.

01:18:32.340 --> 01:18:36.060
Because it's like, how do you try to show

01:18:36.060 --> 01:18:40.050
or evoke an emotion
that is not an emotion?

01:18:40.050 --> 01:18:41.760
- [Garnt] Yeah. Yeah.

01:18:41.760 --> 01:18:45.690
'Cause I remember when one of
my friends from high school,

01:18:45.690 --> 01:18:49.180
he unfortunately passed away very suddenly

01:18:50.258 --> 01:18:51.480
from an illness.

01:18:51.480 --> 01:18:52.313
- [Garnt] Right.

01:18:53.160 --> 01:18:54.750
- You know, I had never experienced that.

01:18:54.750 --> 01:18:57.480
That was the first time
I had experienced death

01:18:57.480 --> 01:19:00.210
in a close, like a real
death in a close vicinity.

01:19:00.210 --> 01:19:01.650
- [Garnt] Yep.

01:19:01.650 --> 01:19:03.783
- And it was so weird because you know,

01:19:04.650 --> 01:19:07.140
media and people who
haven't experienced that

01:19:07.140 --> 01:19:11.040
would lead you to believe
that you go to a funeral.

01:19:11.040 --> 01:19:13.380
- Yeah.
- And everyone's crying.

01:19:13.380 --> 01:19:15.840
Yeah.
- And everyone's sad.

01:19:15.840 --> 01:19:18.480
And I thought I was the weird one

01:19:18.480 --> 01:19:20.673
because I didn't cry at his funeral.

01:19:21.540 --> 01:19:25.140
And I was like, "Am I weird?
Am I being desensitized?"

01:19:25.140 --> 01:19:27.150
I should be sad. I should be crying.

01:19:27.150 --> 01:19:28.710
I should be grieving, you
know, all that kind of stuff.

01:19:28.710 --> 01:19:30.253
And not to say that I wasn't.

01:19:30.253 --> 01:19:33.360
But I think because I'd never experienced

01:19:33.360 --> 01:19:34.620
anything like that before.

01:19:34.620 --> 01:19:38.217
That's when I realized I was
like, "Oh, I'm feeling empty."

01:19:39.084 --> 01:19:44.084
Because that, it's beyond
sadness. It's beyond grief.

01:19:44.730 --> 01:19:47.301
And it was almost this weird thing

01:19:47.301 --> 01:19:51.750
where I didn't start
crying about his death

01:19:51.750 --> 01:19:53.610
until I got home.

01:19:53.610 --> 01:19:54.600
- [Garnt] That was-

01:19:54.600 --> 01:19:56.523
- And that's when it hit.

01:19:56.523 --> 01:19:58.350
- That was the exact same experience

01:19:58.350 --> 01:20:00.338
I had with my grandma as well.

01:20:00.338 --> 01:20:02.197
At the funeral, I was just like,

01:20:02.197 --> 01:20:05.100
"Am I broken? Am I a broken human being?"

01:20:05.100 --> 01:20:05.933
I feel nothing.

01:20:05.933 --> 01:20:08.010
- Yeah, it's like, I
should be crying right now.

01:20:08.010 --> 01:20:09.823
You hear back on like, you know,

01:20:09.823 --> 01:20:11.370
I was hearing back on my friend's life

01:20:11.370 --> 01:20:14.640
and hearing speeches from
my classmates and whatnot.

01:20:14.640 --> 01:20:18.240
And I was just like, "Why am
I not crying? Am I weird?"

01:20:18.240 --> 01:20:19.080
- [Garnt] Yeah.

01:20:19.080 --> 01:20:22.980
- And then it's like, you
grieve, everyone's sad.

01:20:22.980 --> 01:20:25.173
And then I went home and I remember,

01:20:26.820 --> 01:20:29.310
I went into my room and I lay on the bed

01:20:29.310 --> 01:20:31.800
and then I just broke down crying.

01:20:31.800 --> 01:20:34.350
And it's like, "Oh, that's
what that feeling is."

01:20:34.350 --> 01:20:35.183
And it's like,

01:20:35.183 --> 01:20:38.910
I personally have never
seen a piece of fiction

01:20:38.910 --> 01:20:41.430
that can properly evoke that emotion.

01:20:41.430 --> 01:20:43.713
Like it's, I don't
know, it's weird to say.

01:20:43.713 --> 01:20:46.320
It's not like it's faking an emotion

01:20:46.320 --> 01:20:48.563
or anything like that,
when it comes to fiction.

01:20:49.620 --> 01:20:52.260
I wouldn't say it's like...
it's not the correct emotion.

01:20:52.260 --> 01:20:53.093
- [Garnt] Yeah. I feel.

01:20:53.093 --> 01:20:53.926
- And I think that's just because

01:20:53.926 --> 01:20:58.926
it's just so incredibly difficult
to show that real emotion,

01:20:58.950 --> 01:21:01.020
especially when it's with
a bunch of characters

01:21:01.020 --> 01:21:03.180
that you didn't spend your entire

01:21:03.180 --> 01:21:05.215
fucking high school life with.

01:21:05.215 --> 01:21:08.010
- Exactly, so like personal question.

01:21:08.010 --> 01:21:09.710
What's the most you've ever cried

01:21:09.710 --> 01:21:12.060
to a piece of fiction at all?

01:21:12.060 --> 01:21:14.160
- The most?
- Yeah.

01:21:14.160 --> 01:21:16.770
- Probably the second half
of "Clannad: After Story"

01:21:16.770 --> 01:21:21.000
The last six episodes, I was like...

01:21:21.000 --> 01:21:25.286
Episode 14, 15, I'm
obviously not gonna spoil it.

01:21:25.286 --> 01:21:26.820
- [Garnt] Yeah. (laughs)

01:21:26.820 --> 01:21:29.670
- Around episode 14, 15
of "Clannad: After Story"

01:21:29.670 --> 01:21:33.120
something happens, and it's
like, you break down crying.

01:21:33.120 --> 01:21:34.687
And you think to yourself,

01:21:34.687 --> 01:21:36.780
"Okay, it's all out of my system."

01:21:36.780 --> 01:21:38.250
And then the next episode starts

01:21:38.250 --> 01:21:41.790
and it's just like, fuck man, why?

01:21:41.790 --> 01:21:43.197
And then it's just that,

01:21:43.197 --> 01:21:45.300
for the rest of the
episodes until it's over,

01:21:45.300 --> 01:21:47.100
and you're just a fucking mess.

01:21:47.100 --> 01:21:48.475
- I just cry at everything.

01:21:48.475 --> 01:21:50.970
A lot of (indistinct), stuff
that isn't even sad, I cry.

01:21:50.970 --> 01:21:51.849
- Like what?

01:21:51.849 --> 01:21:52.682
- I don't know.

01:21:52.682 --> 01:21:54.360
Becky will be fighting,
and I'll hear my name

01:21:54.360 --> 01:21:55.629
and I'll just start crying.

01:21:55.629 --> 01:21:58.260
(both laugh)

01:21:58.260 --> 01:22:00.600
Yeah, it depends on my mood, right.

01:22:00.600 --> 01:22:02.520
Some days I'm like a
fucking rock and it's like,

01:22:02.520 --> 01:22:05.153
it could be like the worst
thing on earth and I'll be like.

01:22:06.030 --> 01:22:08.010
- It's really weird
'cause I've found myself,

01:22:08.010 --> 01:22:09.540
and I think this is healthy

01:22:09.540 --> 01:22:13.020
because I found myself more easily crying

01:22:13.020 --> 01:22:15.540
towards pieces of media and
fictional pieces of media

01:22:15.540 --> 01:22:17.820
now than I did like five-

01:22:17.820 --> 01:22:18.653
- Oh God, yeah.

01:22:18.653 --> 01:22:20.220
- Five years ago?
- I cry at everything.

01:22:20.220 --> 01:22:21.053
- Yeah.

01:22:21.053 --> 01:22:24.840
And I thing the one that
broke the camels back

01:22:24.840 --> 01:22:26.730
was like, "Anohana".

01:22:26.730 --> 01:22:27.930
- I cried a lot at "Anohana".

01:22:27.930 --> 01:22:28.763
- Yeah.

01:22:28.763 --> 01:22:30.100
- I think before "Anohana",

01:22:30.100 --> 01:22:35.100
I don't think I had ever
cried watching an anime.

01:22:36.270 --> 01:22:37.450
I'm trying to think back.
- For me it was weird.

01:22:37.450 --> 01:22:41.520
It's like very early on when
I was watching a lot of anime,

01:22:41.520 --> 01:22:43.500
'cause I think I first cried at "Clannad"

01:22:43.500 --> 01:22:46.582
and then it was just like
a chain reaction of like...

01:22:46.582 --> 01:22:47.923
and then I watched "Anohana"
and then I watched "Air"

01:22:47.923 --> 01:22:49.863
and then I watch all these
shows that made you cry.

01:22:49.863 --> 01:22:50.730
- [Garnt] Yeah yeah, yeah.

01:22:50.730 --> 01:22:53.080
- And then for a while I had
this blank period where I-

01:22:53.080 --> 01:22:54.180
- It's 'cause you exhausted yourself.

01:22:54.180 --> 01:22:57.030
- Maybe, and then the one
that broke the camels back

01:22:57.030 --> 01:22:58.585
for me was "Maquia".

01:22:58.585 --> 01:22:59.583
- "Maquia", ah.

01:22:59.583 --> 01:23:00.417
- "Angel Beats" made me cry a lot.

01:23:00.417 --> 01:23:02.077
- "Angel Beats" made me
cry, but I didn't cry.

01:23:02.077 --> 01:23:05.280
There was so many sad shows
that people would like cry.

01:23:05.280 --> 01:23:07.680
I didn't cry at the end
of "Your lie in April",

01:23:07.680 --> 01:23:08.880
even though a lot of people did.

01:23:08.880 --> 01:23:10.204
- I didn't either.

01:23:10.204 --> 01:23:11.037
- I don't know, and I was like,

01:23:11.037 --> 01:23:12.410
"Am I weird for thinking that?

01:23:12.410 --> 01:23:14.790
Am I just like overexposed
to this kind of media?"

01:23:14.790 --> 01:23:18.360
And then I watched "Maquia"
on a fucking plane,

01:23:18.360 --> 01:23:20.799
tiny screen like this
with shitty headphones.

01:23:20.799 --> 01:23:22.623
- Crying in warm pee.
- Yeah.

01:23:22.623 --> 01:23:25.140
And crying to three
pixels, and I was like...

01:23:25.140 --> 01:23:26.877
And then the ending to
that just destroyed me.

01:23:26.877 --> 01:23:29.310
I was like, "Why is it this one

01:23:29.310 --> 01:23:30.780
that made me cry after all this time?"

01:23:30.780 --> 01:23:33.390
- It's weird because
before, anytime I would cry,

01:23:33.390 --> 01:23:34.860
just cry towards something,

01:23:34.860 --> 01:23:37.200
that thing would be really,
really fucking special

01:23:37.200 --> 01:23:39.390
to break down the brick wall that I am.

01:23:39.390 --> 01:23:41.400
But nowadays-
- You stone of a man.

01:23:41.400 --> 01:23:43.590
The obelisk known as Garnt's emotions.

01:23:43.590 --> 01:23:45.750
- Exactly, but nowadays,
because I cry way more easily.

01:23:45.750 --> 01:23:48.420
I dunno, it's weird,
sometimes I have empty cries

01:23:48.420 --> 01:23:50.340
where I cry and I'm just like, it's over,

01:23:50.340 --> 01:23:51.390
and then I feel nothing.

01:23:51.390 --> 01:23:53.370
It's just like, I dunno, it's weird.

01:23:53.370 --> 01:23:55.980
- I'm like, I cry and I feel amazing.

01:23:55.980 --> 01:23:56.813
- [Garnt] Yeah, right.

01:23:56.813 --> 01:23:57.810
- I just do it.
- It's like a release.

01:23:57.810 --> 01:23:59.040
- Like I order a McDonald's the other day,

01:23:59.040 --> 01:24:00.630
and I was like, "Why did
I do this?", I cried.

01:24:00.630 --> 01:24:02.280
- I fucking cried to "Demon Slayer"

01:24:02.280 --> 01:24:04.020
And I'm just like, "Why
did I fucking cry..."

01:24:04.020 --> 01:24:05.483
- I get it, I get it, I get it.

01:24:06.570 --> 01:24:09.631
The moment I feel sad, I'm
just like, (imitates crying).

01:24:09.631 --> 01:24:10.687
(Joey imitates crying)

01:24:10.687 --> 01:24:12.107
(Garnt imitates crying)

01:24:12.107 --> 01:24:14.733
- I just get it over
with man. I just do it.

01:24:15.750 --> 01:24:17.400
- Have you ever had those cries though,

01:24:17.400 --> 01:24:20.340
where it doesn't feel
like you've released?

01:24:20.340 --> 01:24:21.810
Where you just feel shittier?

01:24:21.810 --> 01:24:23.340
- Are we talking about edging with tears?

01:24:23.340 --> 01:24:25.560
- Not edging, you cry and then you-

01:24:25.560 --> 01:24:26.940
- And then I climax with tears?

01:24:26.940 --> 01:24:28.650
- No, there's those times where, you know,

01:24:28.650 --> 01:24:30.000
you'd watch something really sad

01:24:30.000 --> 01:24:31.920
and then you just let the emotions out.

01:24:31.920 --> 01:24:34.110
And then after your tears have subsided,

01:24:34.110 --> 01:24:36.900
you're just like, "Whew. All
right. I'm glad that's out."

01:24:36.900 --> 01:24:38.160
You know, I feel good.

01:24:38.160 --> 01:24:40.020
All of my emotions, all my
emotional baggage is out.

01:24:40.020 --> 01:24:42.870
And then there are some times
where you would start crying,

01:24:42.870 --> 01:24:44.280
and then once the tears have subsided,

01:24:44.280 --> 01:24:46.950
you're just like, "Man, now I'm more sad

01:24:46.950 --> 01:24:48.330
than I was before I started crying."

01:24:48.330 --> 01:24:51.030
- That's like when I was 15 with breakups.

01:24:51.030 --> 01:24:52.500
I'd cry and I'd feel worse.

01:24:52.500 --> 01:24:53.520
- Oh, yeah yeah, yeah.

01:24:53.520 --> 01:24:55.835
- Why did she leave me? (imitates crying)

01:24:55.835 --> 01:24:57.796
(Garnt laughs)

01:24:57.796 --> 01:24:59.010
And you know, getting back to funerals.

01:24:59.010 --> 01:25:01.386
I wouldn't... like even if I wasn't,

01:25:01.386 --> 01:25:03.120
'cause you know, sometimes
when you're like 10,

01:25:03.120 --> 01:25:05.130
you didn't really
understand what's going on.

01:25:05.130 --> 01:25:06.240
And then maybe when you get older,

01:25:06.240 --> 01:25:08.347
you're like 15, 16 and it's like,

01:25:08.347 --> 01:25:10.950
"Oh, it's this person
that you barely ever met,

01:25:10.950 --> 01:25:13.890
but you have to 'cause
you're all connected."

01:25:13.890 --> 01:25:15.600
I wouldn't know them so I wasn't sad,

01:25:15.600 --> 01:25:17.550
but I would just get, I would just cry,

01:25:17.550 --> 01:25:19.890
'cause I'm like, "Why is
everyone crying? This is so sad."

01:25:19.890 --> 01:25:21.267
- Aw.

01:25:21.267 --> 01:25:22.100
You cry because everyone
around you is crying.

01:25:22.100 --> 01:25:24.420
- Yeah, 'cause if everyone
else is crying around me,

01:25:24.420 --> 01:25:26.914
I'm like, "Fuck, well I gotta do it now."

01:25:26.914 --> 01:25:28.643
Like a psychopath, like Mark Zuckerberg.

01:25:29.675 --> 01:25:32.040
- This is human emotion, I must cry now.

01:25:32.040 --> 01:25:33.510
- Sad.exe.

01:25:33.510 --> 01:25:35.550
- There something about
being around people who,

01:25:35.550 --> 01:25:37.170
when a room is filled with sad energy,

01:25:37.170 --> 01:25:39.270
it just makes me get like that.

01:25:39.270 --> 01:25:41.610
- It depends for me,
because say for example,

01:25:41.610 --> 01:25:42.660
like the "Demon Slayer" movie,

01:25:42.660 --> 01:25:44.820
everyone was crying like fucking
crazy at the end of that.

01:25:44.820 --> 01:25:46.027
And I'm looking around like,

01:25:46.027 --> 01:25:48.297
"Oh, it's now. I have to cry now."

01:25:49.740 --> 01:25:51.360
I can't get the tears out right now.

01:25:51.360 --> 01:25:55.710
- Like to me, I cannot
cry to a piece of media,

01:25:55.710 --> 01:25:56.790
if there's someone else in the room.

01:25:56.790 --> 01:25:58.320
Like, there's...

01:25:58.320 --> 01:25:59.970
- I can't show the manly tears.

01:25:59.970 --> 01:26:01.290
- Wait, wait. Sydney as well?

01:26:01.290 --> 01:26:02.123
- Huh?
- Sydney as well?

01:26:02.123 --> 01:26:03.660
- Especially Sydney.
- What?

01:26:03.660 --> 01:26:04.594
- Really?
- Do you know why?

01:26:04.594 --> 01:26:05.427
- 'Cause she'll be like,

01:26:05.427 --> 01:26:08.225
"Oh baby man, you want a
little." (imitates crying)

01:26:08.225 --> 01:26:09.060
- No, no, no, no, no, no.

01:26:09.060 --> 01:26:12.030
Because, 10 minutes before the tears

01:26:12.030 --> 01:26:13.740
even start forming in my eyes,

01:26:13.740 --> 01:26:16.050
she's bawling her eyes out already.

01:26:16.050 --> 01:26:16.883
She is, Sydney's...

01:26:16.883 --> 01:26:18.300
- You're on cleanup duty.
- Yeah yeah, yeah.

01:26:18.300 --> 01:26:21.510
- Sydney is so emotionally receptive,

01:26:21.510 --> 01:26:24.480
that she will start crying five minutes

01:26:24.480 --> 01:26:27.127
before the sad moments happen
and she'll be like in tears.

01:26:27.127 --> 01:26:28.748
- Oh my God.

01:26:28.748 --> 01:26:31.380
- Yeah.

01:26:31.380 --> 01:26:34.050
If I'm watching with Sydney, I
am on emotional cleanup duty.

01:26:34.050 --> 01:26:37.110
I'm like, "Oh, it's
okay baby. Don't worry."

01:26:37.110 --> 01:26:40.118
I'm like, baby, I didn't
even get my point.

01:26:40.118 --> 01:26:41.530
I didn't even like...

01:26:41.530 --> 01:26:43.207
- Yeah, I guess you can't really be like,

01:26:43.207 --> 01:26:47.400
"Oh baby, are you okay?" (imitates crying)

01:26:47.400 --> 01:26:49.170
Hold on, gimme a second. (imitates crying)

01:26:49.170 --> 01:26:50.400
- You've heard about relationships

01:26:50.400 --> 01:26:53.340
where the guy comes too
fast and then it ruins it.

01:26:53.340 --> 01:26:55.514
What about the one who cries too fast?

01:26:55.514 --> 01:26:56.844
I can't get my tears in.

01:26:56.844 --> 01:27:00.270
She's already decided it's
over before I've even started.

01:27:00.270 --> 01:27:01.443
- 'Cause I remember,

01:27:02.917 --> 01:27:05.430
"Your Name", I cried like a fucking baby,

01:27:05.430 --> 01:27:06.570
the first time I watched "Your Name".

01:27:06.570 --> 01:27:08.827
And it wasn't even because it was sad.

01:27:08.827 --> 01:27:10.140
"Your Name" was to me,

01:27:10.140 --> 01:27:12.210
the reason it's one of
my favorite anime films

01:27:12.210 --> 01:27:15.030
is 'cause to me it's like
the perfect cinema experience

01:27:15.030 --> 01:27:17.640
where there are so many
things happening on screen

01:27:17.640 --> 01:27:20.560
that there's so many emotions

01:27:21.840 --> 01:27:23.970
that I just get so absorbed

01:27:23.970 --> 01:27:25.830
that my body doesn't know how to react,

01:27:25.830 --> 01:27:27.510
other than just crying.

01:27:27.510 --> 01:27:28.590
Sometimes I get emotional

01:27:28.590 --> 01:27:30.928
and I don't know what to
do with it, and I cry.

01:27:30.928 --> 01:27:32.105
- It's like an overwhelmed cry.

01:27:32.105 --> 01:27:33.360
- Yeah, it's like an overwhelmed cry.

01:27:33.360 --> 01:27:35.022
- Music normally does that for me?

01:27:35.022 --> 01:27:37.272
I fucking cry at like
an E key. I don't know.

01:27:39.090 --> 01:27:39.923
It's always the music for me.

01:27:39.923 --> 01:27:43.110
- First note to "Black
Parade". (imitates crying)

01:27:43.110 --> 01:27:45.820
- That is the music, the music
will make me cry instantly.

01:27:45.820 --> 01:27:47.430
Like "My Hero Academia".

01:27:47.430 --> 01:27:49.507
I don't know why I tear
up whenever I fucking hear

01:27:49.507 --> 01:27:51.450
"You Say Run" with (indistinct) screaming.

01:27:51.450 --> 01:27:53.190
I'm like, "Why, what's going on?"

01:27:53.190 --> 01:27:54.030
- Yeah, I don't-
- Really?

01:27:54.030 --> 01:27:56.790
- It's like I've been
programmed to a certain tune,

01:27:56.790 --> 01:27:58.230
I'm like, (imitates crying)

01:27:58.230 --> 01:27:59.520
- It's like Pavlov.

01:27:59.520 --> 01:28:02.010
- Yeah yeah, yeah, I am
literally like a fucking dog.

01:28:02.010 --> 01:28:05.310
- And so I remember second time

01:28:05.310 --> 01:28:07.170
'cause the first time I went by myself.

01:28:07.170 --> 01:28:08.332
- Sorry Mark Zuckerberg,
by the way, watching this.

01:28:08.332 --> 01:28:09.180
(all laugh)

01:28:09.180 --> 01:28:10.680
I know you normally like these segments.

01:28:10.680 --> 01:28:12.000
I know you can't relate to this. Sorry.

01:28:12.000 --> 01:28:13.560
- So the first time I went by myself

01:28:13.560 --> 01:28:14.827
and the second time I was like,

01:28:14.827 --> 01:28:15.810
"Sydney, you gotta see this film."

01:28:15.810 --> 01:28:17.610
It's fucking, fucking amazing film,

01:28:17.610 --> 01:28:18.443
gotta come see it with me."

01:28:18.443 --> 01:28:20.310
And I remember, it was the moment

01:28:20.310 --> 01:28:22.770
just before Radwimps start playing,

01:28:22.770 --> 01:28:25.830
and that is the moment
where I start crying.

01:28:25.830 --> 01:28:28.380
And I remember sitting in this film

01:28:28.380 --> 01:28:29.880
and it was the second time,

01:28:29.880 --> 01:28:31.450
I was getting as emotional,
I was getting as into it,

01:28:31.450 --> 01:28:34.597
I was like getting absorbed
and I'm like, (imitates crying)

01:28:34.597 --> 01:28:36.990
"It's coming, it's coming.
Radwimps about to play."

01:28:36.990 --> 01:28:40.091
And then like a minute
before they start playing,

01:28:40.091 --> 01:28:42.780
I'm just hear, (imitates
crying) next to me.

01:28:42.780 --> 01:28:43.613
I'm like, "Oh God."

01:28:43.613 --> 01:28:47.340
And it just took me out, I'm like...

01:28:47.340 --> 01:28:49.527
of course, it's Sydney
balling her eyes out.

01:28:49.527 --> 01:28:52.920
But yeah, that's why,
as much as I love Sydney

01:28:52.920 --> 01:28:54.960
if I'm watching a sad thing,

01:28:54.960 --> 01:28:56.760
if I want to have an emotional release,

01:28:56.760 --> 01:28:57.933
I cannot watch it with her in the room.

01:28:57.933 --> 01:28:59.550
- It's like, "Shut the fuck up".

01:28:59.550 --> 01:29:01.020
- I'm like, "Sydney, can
you stop being emotional

01:29:01.020 --> 01:29:02.400
for one second?"

01:29:02.400 --> 01:29:04.920
- Did you watch his new movie?

01:29:04.920 --> 01:29:06.048
- His, "Weathering with You"?

01:29:06.048 --> 01:29:07.464
- Oh, "Weathering with You".

01:29:07.464 --> 01:29:08.297
Yeah, "Weathering with You"

01:29:08.297 --> 01:29:09.775
- "Weathering with you"?
Yes, I did watch it.

01:29:09.775 --> 01:29:10.640
- Did you cry?

01:29:10.640 --> 01:29:11.473
- I did not cry at that.

01:29:11.473 --> 01:29:14.273
- Did you cry at, who's the
other director who's good?

01:29:14.273 --> 01:29:15.106
- Mamoru Hosoda.
- Mamoru Hosoda

01:29:15.106 --> 01:29:16.677
- Yeah, what's his? "Belle".

01:29:17.730 --> 01:29:21.040
- I thought "Belle" was okay.

01:29:21.040 --> 01:29:22.380
(Joey gasps)

01:29:22.380 --> 01:29:23.730
It was...

01:29:23.730 --> 01:29:25.860
- Would you say it was mid?

01:29:25.860 --> 01:29:27.210
- Okay, here's...

01:29:27.210 --> 01:29:28.318
- I watched it by the way.

01:29:28.318 --> 01:29:29.151
- You watched it?

01:29:29.151 --> 01:29:29.984
- I haven't seen it yet.

01:29:29.984 --> 01:29:33.033
- What did you think of it?

01:29:33.033 --> 01:29:35.460
Okay, did you watch it in cinemas?

01:29:35.460 --> 01:29:36.330
- No.

01:29:36.330 --> 01:29:37.860
- Okay, I feel like that's a movie

01:29:37.860 --> 01:29:39.720
you have to experience in cinemas

01:29:39.720 --> 01:29:44.130
because everyone I've talked
to who has seen "Belle",

01:29:44.130 --> 01:29:48.210
they've talked about how
it's a fucking incredible

01:29:48.210 --> 01:29:52.126
cinema experience with
the sound and the music.

01:29:52.126 --> 01:29:54.120
There are definitely scenes in "Belle"

01:29:54.120 --> 01:29:55.740
where I'm like, "I get that".

01:29:55.740 --> 01:29:58.800
It feels like, especially
with the musical scenes,

01:29:58.800 --> 01:30:00.690
the musical numbers, it
feels like these scenes

01:30:00.690 --> 01:30:04.183
were made to be experienced in a theater,

01:30:04.183 --> 01:30:06.543
with the surrounds sound and everything.

01:30:07.440 --> 01:30:10.500
In terms of the plots and everything else,

01:30:10.500 --> 01:30:13.620
it was not his greatest
movie, in my opinion.

01:30:13.620 --> 01:30:14.910
- Was it one of those movies though,

01:30:14.910 --> 01:30:17.071
that it was like cry bait?

01:30:17.071 --> 01:30:17.904
- Yeah.

01:30:17.904 --> 01:30:20.880
- So it was like the...
because that's the thing.

01:30:20.880 --> 01:30:22.470
- I felt like it didn't earn it.

01:30:22.470 --> 01:30:23.640
- But that's the thing is like,

01:30:23.640 --> 01:30:25.620
sometimes it's so weird with fiction

01:30:25.620 --> 01:30:27.810
that is obvious cry bait.

01:30:27.810 --> 01:30:29.340
Where it's like, sometimes,

01:30:29.340 --> 01:30:31.650
yes, I will buy into the
cry bait very happily.

01:30:31.650 --> 01:30:32.483
Thank you very much.

01:30:32.483 --> 01:30:34.027
And then there are other
times where it's like,

01:30:34.027 --> 01:30:36.330
"Okay, you don't have to push
this in my face this much.

01:30:36.330 --> 01:30:39.300
I'll cry when I wanna
cry or if I can cry."

01:30:39.300 --> 01:30:42.870
- They have a digital world
in the show and a movie.

01:30:42.870 --> 01:30:45.600
I just wasn't invested in this world.

01:30:45.600 --> 01:30:47.400
I just didn't think it was like,

01:30:47.400 --> 01:30:51.033
I couldn't see it being a
thing or why people would care,

01:30:52.020 --> 01:30:54.127
'cause it was like, we're just
gonna make an online world

01:30:54.127 --> 01:30:56.520
where you can be anything except you can't

01:30:56.520 --> 01:30:58.706
and your avatars chosen for you, and also,

01:30:58.706 --> 01:31:00.270
there seems to be like a class system

01:31:00.270 --> 01:31:02.670
where some people are more important

01:31:02.670 --> 01:31:03.780
than others in this world.

01:31:03.780 --> 01:31:04.947
- Why does that just
sound like "Summer Wars"?

01:31:04.947 --> 01:31:05.780
- And I was like this is-

01:31:05.780 --> 01:31:07.474
- It is exactly "Summer Wars".

01:31:07.474 --> 01:31:09.500
- Oh, okay.
- Yeah.

01:31:09.500 --> 01:31:11.340
- I was like, how do you know
it's a Hosoda Mamoru movie?

01:31:11.340 --> 01:31:12.860
- He's made the same movie again,

01:31:12.860 --> 01:31:14.700
with "Beauty and the Beast" this time.

01:31:14.700 --> 01:31:15.533
- Oh my God.

01:31:15.533 --> 01:31:16.366
- Yeah, it was "Beauty and the Beast".

01:31:16.366 --> 01:31:18.270
That's what I was also like, what's this?

01:31:18.270 --> 01:31:20.097
I wasn't... It was okay.

01:31:20.097 --> 01:31:21.921
- It was okay.

01:31:21.921 --> 01:31:23.100
(all laugh)

01:31:23.100 --> 01:31:24.317
I agree with you.

01:31:24.317 --> 01:31:26.610
- You know what I watched in the cinema?

01:31:26.610 --> 01:31:28.110
- What?
- The Batman.

01:31:28.110 --> 01:31:28.943
- Oh, how was it?

01:31:28.943 --> 01:31:30.120
- Very, very good.
- Really?

01:31:30.120 --> 01:31:30.953
- Have you watched it yet?

01:31:30.953 --> 01:31:32.310
- No, no yet.
- Was it three hours?

01:31:32.310 --> 01:31:33.143
- Yes.

01:31:33.143 --> 01:31:34.260
- Okay.
- And I loved it.

01:31:34.260 --> 01:31:36.240
- How was Robert Pattinson in it?

01:31:36.240 --> 01:31:37.530
- Delightful, just a treat.
- Yeah?

01:31:37.530 --> 01:31:39.536
- What a great guy, what a great guy.

01:31:39.536 --> 01:31:41.507
- What a bloke.

01:31:41.507 --> 01:31:42.795
- I saw a meme the other day.

01:31:42.795 --> 01:31:47.570
It was like 2010, women
fawning over Robert Pattinson.

01:31:47.570 --> 01:31:50.326
It was like 2020, men fawning
over Robert Pattinson.

01:31:50.326 --> 01:31:51.240
(Joey laughs)

01:31:51.240 --> 01:31:52.500
It's so true, dude.

01:31:52.500 --> 01:31:53.333
- Hell yeah.

01:31:53.333 --> 01:31:54.517
- It's good, it's a good
movie, it's good movie.

01:31:54.517 --> 01:31:57.723
- Is it a good movie or
is it a good Batman movie?

01:31:59.490 --> 01:32:02.250
- I think it's not that
much of a Batman movie.

01:32:02.250 --> 01:32:04.230
- Really?
- Really?

01:32:04.230 --> 01:32:06.120
- I'd give it an 8.5.

01:32:06.120 --> 01:32:09.390
- Because I'm like one of the weird people

01:32:09.390 --> 01:32:12.690
who really don't give that
much of a shit about Batman.

01:32:12.690 --> 01:32:14.280
I don't know, to me, it's just...

01:32:14.280 --> 01:32:16.710
- I really like this
portrayal by Robert Pattinson.

01:32:16.710 --> 01:32:17.850
- Yeah.
- I thought-

01:32:17.850 --> 01:32:19.300
- Is it kind of more like...

01:32:19.300 --> 01:32:23.808
Is it kinda more like on the
Joker side of storytelling?

01:32:23.808 --> 01:32:24.690
- No, no.

01:32:24.690 --> 01:32:26.220
- Or is it more like a Batman being-

01:32:26.220 --> 01:32:27.487
- Oh, oh, well I suppose,

01:32:27.487 --> 01:32:28.633
if that's the scale that we're going with,

01:32:28.633 --> 01:32:30.610
I guess it would lean more
towards the Joker side.

01:32:30.610 --> 01:32:31.890
- Okay. Okay. Yeah.

01:32:31.890 --> 01:32:34.770
- But I wouldn't compare
it to the Joker either.

01:32:34.770 --> 01:32:39.770
It's more like they clearly
wanna tell Batman as a character

01:32:40.770 --> 01:32:43.550
through this kind of
somewhat realistic lens

01:32:43.550 --> 01:32:46.200
of like, if Batman was a real person,

01:32:46.200 --> 01:32:48.240
he would be a fucking weirdo.

01:32:48.240 --> 01:32:49.560
- More like a human drama side of things.

01:32:49.560 --> 01:32:52.680
- Well it's kind of
detective movie, but also,

01:32:52.680 --> 01:32:55.080
they don't shy away from
showing Batman as being,

01:32:55.080 --> 01:32:56.195
having a lot of issues.

01:32:56.195 --> 01:32:57.028
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

01:32:57.028 --> 01:32:58.080
- Like the man's got problems.

01:32:58.080 --> 01:32:59.010
- Yeah. Yeah.

01:32:59.010 --> 01:33:00.180
- You know, and...

01:33:00.180 --> 01:33:01.020
- More money, more problems.

01:33:01.020 --> 01:33:02.675
- Yeah, dude.

01:33:02.675 --> 01:33:04.860
I liked the villain. I
thought it was pretty good.

01:33:04.860 --> 01:33:06.250
- The Riddler this time.
- The Riddler. Yeah.

01:33:06.250 --> 01:33:07.313
- Oh, it's Riddler, oh shit.

01:33:07.313 --> 01:33:08.203
- I thought they had a good,

01:33:08.203 --> 01:33:11.253
a really interesting take
on the Riddler that I liked.

01:33:12.210 --> 01:33:13.264
I just had fun.

01:33:13.264 --> 01:33:15.270
I was there for three hours.

01:33:15.270 --> 01:33:16.230
Maybe towards the end,

01:33:16.230 --> 01:33:18.090
